From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:40:47 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: leds: qcom-lpg: Document PMK8850 PWM

The PMK8850 PMIC, used on Glymur and Kaanapali boards, has a PWM block
that is compatible with the PMK8550 PWM. With the PMK8550 match data,
leds-qcom-lpg drives channel 0 of the PMK8850 PWM as the display
backlight on the Microsoft Surface Laptop 8.

Document the PMK8850 PWM compatible, with the PMK8550 PWM as fallback.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/leds-qcom-lpg.yaml | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/leds-qcom-lpg.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/leds-qcom-lpg.yaml
index 3da0fe532e7..e018f1f3532 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/leds-qcom-lpg.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/leds-qcom-lpg.yaml
@@ -49,6 +49,10 @@ properties:
           - enum:
               - qcom,pm8937-pwm
           - const: qcom,pm8916-pwm
+      - items:
+          - enum:
+              - qcom,pmk8850-pwm
+          - const: qcom,pmk8550-pwm
 
   "#pwm-cells":
     const: 2
-- 
